# Animation & Motion Rules

## Core Rules
- Only animate transform and opacity — never width, height, top, left, or layout properties
- GPU-accelerated properties only — no layout-triggering animations
- All whileInView must use viewport={{ once: true }}
- Always respect prefers-reduced-motion
- Lenis is globally configured — never add a second scroll instance
- Target 60fps — if in doubt, simplify

## Framer Motion Patterns
- Scroll-linked values: useScroll + useTransform
- Viewport entry: useInView + motion variants
- Weighted scroll: useSpring({ stiffness: 100, damping: 30 })
- Stagger cascades: staggerChildren 0.12-0.15, delayChildren 0.3-0.4
- Cinematic ease: [0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1] or [0.19, 1, 0.22, 1] for dramatic reveals
- Duration: 0.8-1.4s for premium feel — never fast or bouncy

## Animation Types
- Image reveal: clipPath inset(100% 0% 0% 0%) → inset(0% 0% 0% 0%)
- Gold line draw: width 0 → 96px on useInView
- Floating orbs: animate={{ y: [0, -8, 0] }} duration 6-13s infinite
- Breathing glow: animate={{ scale: [1, 1.2, 1], opacity: [0.3, 0.5, 0.3] }} duration 4s
- Shimmer: backgroundPosition "200% auto" → "0% auto" infinite

## Gradient Transitions
- Never hard edges between sections
- Always route: cream → blush → teal (never cream → teal directly)
- Bridge height: h-32 minimum, h-48 for large color shifts
- Always pointer-events-none on bridges

## Canvas Hero
- Preload all WebP frames before scrubbing
- Use requestAnimationFrame for frame drawing loop
- Map scroll progress to frame index: floor(progress × (totalFrames - 1))
- Handle resize for high-DPI canvas clarity